Warhammer 40k Inquisitor Mota is an  action RPG which faithfully evokes the  atmosphere of the grim 41st millennium  it's an intense experience focusing on a  gameplay with a spectacular display of  destruction recalls the sense of  constant warfare take a look at your  surroundings let the glorious carnage  commence in the name of the Emperor and  know that nothing can survive the  devastation you are going to unleash the  new in-house developed cool tech engine  combines with updated physics grants of  welcome diversity in how different types  of attacks affect the environment the  environment also has a significant role  in the gameplay Inquisitor Mata is an  action RPG with some fundamental  improvements and one of these new  additions is the cover system which  grants a tactical layer to the game  covers are fixed obstacles to provide a  more realistic approach to the  firefights the first rule of the cover  system is that both inquisitors and  their enemies can use certain objects to  shield themselves from hostile attacks  rule number two since the cover is also  cost the environment it can be destroyed  depending on their size creatures can  use obstacles to mitigate incoming  damage the type and the material will  determine how much damage a cover can  absorb most of the obstacles can be  destroyed over time but it also depends  on the weapon of choice bolt ammunition  will break down the barriers gradually  chipping away the defenses on the other  hand class guns disintegrate most covers  with a couple of large glass  under relentless fire even massive  columns can collapse burying Friend or  Foe under the rubble destructible  environment can be either a benefit or  hazard dangerous objects like  pressurized containers can explode upon  impact which in turn will create a  physical blowback effect it is an  effective way to [ __ ] all of the  creatures caught in the blast all-in-all  destructible environment is one of the  key elements in Inquisitor Marta  there'll be some more to follow stay  tuned for more videos and welcome to the  grim world of Warhammer 40k
 

